<report>
<line><title>Simple linear regression</title></line>
<line></line>
<line><b>Equation: </b><in>eq_y</in> <in>eq_x</in></line>
<line></line>
<block name="se">
<line>Standard Error of slope = <inu>slope_err</inu></line>
<line><ci><in>se_pc</in>% CI for population value of slope = <inu>se_from</inu> to <inu>se_to</inu></ci></line>
<line></line>
<line>Correlation coefficient (r) = <inu>se_r</inu> (r<sub>2</sub> = <inu>se_r2</inu>)</line>
<line></line>
<block name="ci">
<line><ci><in>ci_pc</in>% CI for r (Fisher's z transformed) = <inu>ci_from</inu> to <inu>ci_to</inu></ci></line>
<line></line>
<line>t with <in>df</in> DF = <inu>tdf</inu></line>
<line><pval>Two sided <inp>p</inp></pval></line>
<line>Power <in>pwr</in></line>
<line></line>
<line><in>sig</in></line>
</block>
</block>
<block name="notcalc">
<line><warn>SE and CI for slope not calculated when r = 1 or -1</warn></line>
<line><subtotal>Correlation coefficient (r) = <inu>r</inu></subtotal></line>
<line><warn>CI and t for correlation not calculated when r = 1 or -1</warn></line>
</block>
</report>
